    <string name="h3_relay_help">How it works&#10;Queue several segments; each one continues from the last frame of the previous run, so a long clip is built in pieces.&#10;&#10;Using it&#10;1. Turn the switch on&#10;2. Write the prompt, tap Add to queue; each tap is one segment&#10;3. Only the current segment goes to the server; when it finishes the app takes its last frame, moves it into the reference slot and submits the next one&#10;&#10;Notes&#10;· Each segment keeps the settings from the moment you tapped Add (duration, ratio, steps)&#10;· Turning the switch off pauses it; remaining segments are kept and resume when you turn it back on&#10;· Do not swipe the app away while relay runs: frame capture and submission both depend on the phone&#10;· A failed segment stops and waits for you; nothing is skipped&#10;&#10;Related setting&#10;Settings → Relay notification (off by default)&#10;When on, the notification shows how many segments finished and how many remain, with pause and resume;&#10;it also keeps the app alive through long screen-off periods.&#10;Relay works without it, but the system may stop a backgrounded app sooner;&#10;reopening the app continues from the remaining segments.</string>
    <string name="h3_hint_second_pass_steps">2 to 10 steps is recommended; this is the denoise steps of the Turbo second pass.</string>
    <string name="h3_hint_rtx_scale">1.0 means no upscale; 1.2 is 1.2×, 1.5 is 1.5×.</string>
